 ```
 
+## Accounts and authentication
+
+Each person has an account and sees only their own tasks. The page has a sign-up and sign-in form and a sign-out button;
+it keeps the token in `localStorage` and sends it with every request.
+
+- `POST /api/users` with `{ "username", "password" }` creates an account: `201 { "id", "username" }`.
+  The username is lowercased, then must be 3 to 32 characters among `a-z`, `0-9` and `_` (else `400 { "error": "invalid username" }`);
+  one already taken, in any case, is `409 { "error": "username taken" }`. The password must have at least 10 characters
+  (else `400 { "error": "password too short" }`) and at most 256 (`400 password too long`).
+- `POST /api/sessions` with `{ "username", "password" }` signs in: `201 { "token": "…" }`. A wrong username or password is
+  `401 { "error": "invalid credentials" }`, the same answer in both cases. A user can have several sessions; they expire after 30 days.
+- `DELETE /api/sessions` signs out: `204`, and the token stops working. It needs the token like the task routes.
+- Every `/api/tasks` route needs the header `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. A missing, malformed or unknown token is
+  `401 { "error": "authentication required" }`.
+- A task belongs to the user who created it. Reading, changing or deleting a task of someone else is
+  `404 { "error": "task not found" }`, exactly as for a task that does not exist.
+
+How secrets are kept: passwords are hashed with scrypt (`node:crypto`) and a random 16-byte salt per password, and compared in
+constant time. Tokens are 32 random bytes from the OS (`crypto.randomBytes`), shown once; only their SHA-256 is stored.
+No response contains a password or a hash. Tasks created before accounts existed stay in the database (with no owner) but nobody sees them.
+
+Not covered: there is no rate limiting of sign-in attempts, no password reset, and the server speaks plain HTTP: put it behind
+TLS (a reverse proxy) before exposing it.
+
 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON (at most 16 KB; a malformed one is `400 { "error": "invalid JSON" }`). A task is
+`{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+The task routes below all need the `Authorization` header described above and only deal with the signed-in user's tasks.
 
